 I'm glad to continue our discussion about improving your Able-GPT API that integrates GitHub and Notion. Let me address your immediate question about block format handling before diving into the priority list for improvements.

## Handling Block Format Content and Block-to-Markdown Conversion

You're right to consider bidirectional conversion between Markdown and Notion's block format. This would make your API more flexible and universally adaptable. Let's explore how to implement both directions:

### 1. Accepting Notion Block Format Input

Currently, your API accepts markdown text and converts it to Notion blocks. To support direct block format input, you'd need to:

1. Modify your endpoints to accept either markdown text or a JSON array of Notion blocks
2. Add validation to determine which format was provided
3. Skip the conversion step if blocks are already provided

Here's how you could modify your routes:

```javascript
// In page-operations.js or similar files
router.patch("/update-page", async (req, res) => {
  try {
    const { pageId, content, contentFormat = "markdown" } = req.body;

    // Input validation
    if (!pageId || !content) {
      return res.status(400).json({ error: "Missing pageId or content." });
    }

    let contentBlocks;

    // Handle different content formats
    if (contentFormat === "blocks" && Array.isArray(content)) {
      // Content is already in block format
      contentBlocks = content;

      // Validate blocks (you'll need to implement this)
      if (!validateNotionBlocks(contentBlocks)) {
        return res.status(400).json({ 
          error: "Invalid block format. Please check your input." 
        });
      }
    } else {
      // Default: Parse markdown to blocks
      const sanitizedContent = sanitizeInput(content);
      contentBlocks = parseMarkdownToBlocks(sanitizedContent);
    }

    // Rest of your existing code to update the page...
  } catch (error) {
    handleApiError(res, error, "update-page");
  }
});
```

### 2. Converting Notion Blocks to Markdown

For the reverse direction (blocks to markdown), you'll need a new utility function:

```javascript
/**
 * Converts Notion blocks to markdown format
 * @param {Array} blocks - Array of Notion blocks
 * @returns {string} - Markdown representation of the blocks
 */
function blocksToMarkdown(blocks) {
  if (!blocks || !Array.isArray(blocks)) return '';

  return blocks.map(block => {
    switch (block.type) {
      case 'paragraph':
        const paragraphText = extractTextFromRichText(block.paragraph.rich_text);
        return paragraphText ? `${paragraphText}\n\n` : '\n';

      case 'heading_1':
        return `# ${extractTextFromRichText(block.heading_1.rich_text)}\n\n`;

      case 'heading_2':
        return `## ${extractTextFromRichText(block.heading_2.rich_text)}\n\n`;

      case 'heading_3':
        return `### ${extractTextFromRichText(block.heading_3.rich_text)}\n\n`;

      case 'bulleted_list_item':
        return `* ${extractTextFromRichText(block.bulleted_list_item.rich_text)}\n`;

      case 'numbered_list_item':
        return `1. ${extractTextFromRichText(block.numbered_list_item.rich_text)}\n`;

      case 'code':
        return `\`\`\`${block.code.language || 'plain_text'}\n${extractTextFromRichText(block.code.rich_text)}\n\`\`\`\n\n`;

      case 'quote':
        return `> ${extractTextFromRichText(block.quote.rich_text)}\n\n`;

      case 'callout':
        const emoji = block.callout.icon?.emoji || '💡';
        return `> ${emoji} ${extractTextFromRichText(block.callout.rich_text)}\n\n`;

      case 'to_do':
        const checkbox = block.to_do.checked ? '[x]' : '[ ]';
        return `${checkbox} ${extractTextFromRichText(block.to_do.rich_text)}\n`;

      case 'toggle':
        return `>>> ${extractTextFromRichText(block.toggle.rich_text)}\n\n`;

      case 'divider':
        return `---\n\n`;

      // Add other block types as needed

      default:
        return '';
    }
  }).join('');
}

/**
 * Helper function to extract plain text from rich_text array
 * @param {Array} richText - Notion rich_text array
 * @returns {string} - Plain text representation
 */
function extractTextFromRichText(richText) {
  if (!richText || !Array.isArray(richText)) return '';
  return richText.map(rt => rt.plain_text || rt.text?.content || '').join('');
}
```

Then, you could add a new endpoint to fetch page content as markdown:

```javascript
router.get("/page-as-markdown/:id", async (req, res) => {
  try {
    const pageId = req.params.id;

    if (!pageId) {
