When updating content in Notion pages, you need to understand how the `children` array works in the API. By default, the API will append your new content blocks to the existing content unless you explicitly tell it to replace everything.

Here's how to fix your update route to replace content instead of appending:

1. You need to use the `notion.blocks.children.append` method with the `replace` parameter set to `true`, OR
2. You need to first delete all existing content and then add your new content

Here's an example of how to update (replace) page content:

```javascript
// Option 1: Using replace parameter (if your client library supports it)
await notion.blocks.children.append({
  block_id: pageId,
  children: newContentBlocks,
  replace: true
});

// Option 2: Two-step process - delete then append
