# Guide: Testing ChromaDB Integration with Next.js

This guide covers how to set up a proper test environment and implement tests for ChromaDB integration with Next.js applications, focusing specifically on testing functionality for adding entries to ChromaDB.

## Table of Contents
1. [Environment Setup](#environment-setup)
2. [TypeScript Interfaces](#typescript-interfaces)
3. [Mock Implementations](#mock-implementations)
4. [Helper Utilities](#helper-utilities)
5. [Test Implementation](#test-implementation)
   - [Single Entry Test](#single-entry-test)
   - [Metadata Tests](#metadata-tests)
   - [Multiple Entries Test](#multiple-entries-test)
   - [Validation Tests](#validation-tests)
   - [Error Handling Tests](#error-handling-tests)

## Environment Setup

First, install the necessary dependencies:

```bash
npm install --save-dev jest ts-jest @types/jest @testing-library/react @testing-library/jest-dom jest-environment-jsdom
```

Configure Jest for your Next.js project by creating a `jest.config.js` file:

```javascript
// jest.config.js
const nextJest = require('next/jest');

const createJestConfig = nextJest({
  dir: './',
});

const customJestConfig = {
  setupFilesAfterEnv: ['<rootDir>/jest.setup.js'],
  testEnvironment: 'jest-environment-jsdom',
  moduleNameMapper: {
    '^@/(.*)$': '<rootDir>/src/$1',
  },
  collectCoverage: true,
  collectCoverageFrom: [
    'src/**/*.{ts,tsx}',
    '!src/**/*.d.ts',
    '!**/node_modules/**',
  ],
};

module.exports = createJestConfig(customJestConfig);
```

Create a `jest.setup.js` file for additional setup:

```javascript
// jest.setup.js
import '@testing-library/jest-dom';

// Mock the ChromaDB client
jest.mock('@/lib/chroma-client', () => require('@/test/mocks/chroma-client.mock'));

// Global beforeAll and afterAll hooks
beforeAll(() => {
  console.log('Starting ChromaDB integration tests');
});

afterAll(() => {
  console.log('Finished ChromaDB integration tests');
});
```

## TypeScript Interfaces

Define interfaces for your memory items and ChromaDB entities in a file like `src/types/memory.ts`:

```typescript
