  // Get database schema
  const schema = await schemaDetection.getDatabaseSchema(DB_ID);
  // ...use schema for operations
}
```

To implement this strategy effectively, you could:

1. Simplify your OpenAPI specification to describe the general capabilities without detailed property schemas
2. Add a schema discovery endpoint (which you already have via `/notion/databases/getschema`)
3. Document that clients should first fetch the schema and then format their requests accordingly

This would make your API more flexible while significantly reducing the size of your OpenAPI documentation.

