 Yes, I can help you set up an auto-restart mechanism for your API server. I'll provide solutions for both approaches: automatically restarting on file changes and creating a dedicated restart route.

## Option 1: Auto-restart on File Changes with Nodemon

Nodemon is a utility that monitors file changes and automatically restarts your Node.js application:

```javascript
// 1. Install nodemon on your desktop
// npm install -g nodemon

// 2. Modify your package.json to include:
/*
"scripts": {
  "start": "node server.js",
  "dev": "nodemon server.js --watch './**/*.js' --watch './**/*.json'"
}
*/

// 3. Run your server with:
// npm run dev
```

This will automatically restart your server whenever any JavaScript or JSON file changes.

## Option 2: Create a Dedicated Restart Route

You can add a special route to your Express app that triggers a restart:

```javascript
