 Accessing your server console logs from your laptop is an essential part of remote development. Let me show you several options for viewing your server logs remotely.

## Option 1: VS Code's Remote SSH Terminal

The simplest approach is using VS Code's integrated terminal when connected via Remote SSH:

1. Connect to your desktop via VS Code Remote SSH
2. Open a new terminal in VS Code (`Ctrl+` `)
3. Run: `pm2 logs therapy-assistant --lines 100`

This shows the logs directly in your VS Code terminal window. The `--lines 100` flag shows the last 100 log lines.

## Option 2: Real-time Log Streaming with Cloudflare Tunnel

Set up a secure log endpoint in your Express app:

```javascript
const express = require('express');
const app = express();
const fs = require('fs');
const path = require('path');
const { exec } = require('child_process');

// Your existing routes...

// Log streaming endpoint (secure with the same secret)
